<h1>TActiveListBox</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveListBox" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveListBox</tt> is the active counterpart to the original <tt>TListBox</tt> control.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
The <tt>AutoPostBack</tt> property is set to true by default.
Thus, when a list item is clicked a <tt>OnCallback</tt> event is
raised after <tt>OnSelectedIndexChanged</tt> event.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The selection can be changed from the server. Assigning <tt>SelectedIndex</tt>,
<tt>SelectedIndices</tt>, <tt>SelectedValue</tt>, or <tt>SelectedValues</tt> moves the
selection in the browser, subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. A list with a prompt item counts
the prompt outside the index, in the same way a postback does.
</p>

<h2>Changing the items</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Like <a href="?page=ActiveControls.ActiveDropDownList">TActiveDropDownList</a>, a list box
can have its <tt>Items</tt> collection rebuilt during a callback, and the new options
reach the browser with the response.
</p>

<h2>Single and multiple selection</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>SelectionMode</tt> can also change during a callback. Switching to a multiple mode
rewrites the field name so the browser posts an array, and switching back undoes that.
Without the rename a multiple selection would arrive at the server as a single value.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Please refer to the original documentation of <a href="?page=Controls.List">TListBox</a> for usage.
</p>

